QRGuard – Entities and Database
Must have (R1)
Scan – one upload and its result
QRContent – decoded text, is it a link?
URL – full link, scheme, host, real domain
CheckResult – check name, passed?, severity, reason
Verdict – Safe / Suspicious / Dangerous, advice, proceed allowed?
KnownBrand – brand name, official domain
Shortener – shortener domain (e.g. bit.ly)

Relationships

Scan → 1 QRContent
QRContent → 0 or 1 URL
Scan → many CheckResults
Scan → 1 Verdict
Should have (R2)
Organisation – name, type
OfficialDomain – domain, linked organisation
Administrator – username, password hash
MLPrediction – model name, probability

Relationships

Organisation → many OfficialDomains
Administrator → manages many Organisations
Scan → 0 or 1 MLPrediction
Database
Not stored: Scan, QRContent, URL, CheckResult, Verdict, MLPrediction (privacy, NFR-03)
Stored (R1): known_brand, shortener (JSON file in December)
Stored (R2): organisation, official_domain, administrator (SQLite)